# Realm-specific debate scenes: classes, specs, camps and pride. Specialization names are checked
# against the world database; the arguments are period knowledge in new words.

@kind debate

# ======================= Midgard =======================
@realm mid

@topic mid_main_healer
@levels 20-50
@scene healer_or_shaman
@role B class=Healer
@role C class=Shaman
@role D type=*
A: {q} healer or shaman for a group's main heals?
B: healer. bigger heals, group heals, and pac mez on top
C: shaman heals fine and the buffs make every fight shorter
B: shorter fights dont matter if the tank falls over
C: with my buffs and end regen the tank falls over a lot later
D: take both and stop arguing, you two are the best pair in midgard
A: fair, healer and shaman it is

@topic cave_shaman
@levels 20-50
@scene cave_shaman
@role B class=Shaman
@role C type=*
A: is a cave shaman just a damage class that can heal a bit?
B: subterranean is diseases and damage over time, it changes the whole fight
C: groups want heals from a shaman, not dots
B: groups want things dead. a diseased target heals for less
C: tell that to the tank at a quarter health
B: the tank was at a quarter because the mob lived too long

@topic skald_role
@levels 20-50
@scene skald_role
@role B class=Skald
@role C type=NoLifer,Leveler
A: are skalds just speed bots with axes?
B: battlesongs is more than speed, the shouts hurt
C: in a group the speed is the reason we invite you
B: i know, and i will play it, but let me swing sometimes
C: swing all you want, just keep the song up
B: deal. song up, axes out

@topic thane_identity
@levels 20-50
@scene thane_identity
@role B class=Thane
@role C type=*
A: is a thane a tank or a caster?
B: both. stormcalling hits hard and i can still take a beating
C: jack of all trades, master of none
B: the master of none still kills you while you think about it
C: fair, the lightning is no joke
A: thane life sounds fun honestly

@topic sm_rm
@levels 35-50
@scene sm_or_rm
@role B class=Spiritmaster
@role C class=Runemaster
A: spiritmaster or runemaster for a group?
B: spiritmaster, the pet tanks and keeps the adds off us
C: runemaster, the damage is the reason fights end
B: fights end faster when nobody gets added on
C: fights end fastest when the target is already dead
B: fine. dead things dont add, i give you that

@topic shadowblade_weapons
@levels 20-50
@scene sb_weapons
@role B class=Shadowblade
@role C type=*
A: left axe or two-handed for a shadowblade?
B: left axe, the extra swings stack the poison faster
C: the big two-hander opener drops casters before they move
B: one big hit, then youre just a weak fighter in the open
C: one big hit is all you need on a caster
A: left axe, i like stabbing a lot

@topic warrior_boring
@levels 20-50
@scene warrior_boring
@role B class=Warrior
@role C type=Daredevil
A: are warriors the most boring class in midgard?
B: boring is the group never dying because i hold everything
C: you hit buttons and get hit, where is the excitement
B: the excitement is watching you live because of me
C: ok thats a good comeback
A: respect the warrior

@topic mid_40s
@levels 38-50
@scene spindel_or_varulv
@role B type=Leveler
@role C type=Explorer,Daredevil
A: spindelhalla or varulvhamn for the 40s?
B: spindelhalla, the halls are packed with camps and the xp is steady
C: varulvhamn, fewer groups fighting over the same pulls
B: fewer groups because the wolves hit like trains
C: and drop like trains too
B: enjoy the corpse runs

@topic aegir
@levels 30-50
@scene aegir_or_classic
@role B type=Explorer
@role C type=Leveler
A: anyone level on aegir or is it all spindelhalla?
B: aegir is gorgeous and the camps are empty, try iarnwood
C: empty because the old camps are proven
B: proven and crowded. i like having a camp to myself
C: i like knowing exactly what i will get
A: trying gripklosa this weekend, will report back

# ======================= Albion =======================
@realm alb

@topic paladin
@levels 20-50
@scene paladin_worth
@role B class=Paladin
@role C type=Leveler
A: is a paladin worth inviting over another fighter?
B: the chants carry the whole group, endurance alone wins long fights
C: the damage is low though
B: the damage is low because im busy keeping you running
C: twisting chants is hard to do well
A: a good paladin is gold then

@topic albion_casters
@levels 35-50
@scene wiz_or_sorc
@role B class=Wizard
@role C class=Sorcerer
@role D class=Theurgist
A: best caster in albion, go
B: wizard. fire, earth, cold, things die from across the room
C: sorcerer. i mez the room, then your fire actually lands
D: theurgist. my pets do the job while you two argue
B: pets die to one area spell
D: and come right back
A: so the answer is all three, with a cleric

@topic minstrel
@levels 20-50
@scene minstrel
@role B class=Minstrel
@role C type=*
A: are minstrels a speed bot or a real class?
B: speed, mez, charm, and a sword. very real class
C: in a group i mainly want the speed though
B: i know. i also want respect
C: here is your respect, now speed please
A: lol, sing on

@topic reaver_merc
@levels 20-50
@scene reaver_or_merc
@role B class=Reaver
@role C class=Mercenary
A: reaver or mercenary for a new fighter?
B: reaver, flex has reach and soulrending makes fights weird for the enemy
C: merc, dual wield and evade, fast and honest
B: honest and predictable
C: predictable and alive
A: trying reaver, i like weird

@topic alb_40s
@levels 38-50
@scene barrows_or_avalon
@role B type=Leveler
@role C type=Explorer
A: barrows or the avalon isle camps for the 40s?
B: stonehenge barrows, everyone knows the pulls and the xp is fast
C: avalon isle, the drakoran camps are open and the view is better
B: the view doesnt give you levels
C: the empty camp does
A: barrows tonight, avalon on the weekend

@topic scouts
@levels 35-50
@scene scout_range
@role B class=Scout
@role C type=*
A: the other realms say scouts are overpowered at range
B: the other realms have never tried to keep a scout alive up close
C: we do hit hard from very far away though
B: only if they stand in the open. nobody should stand in the open
A: so the advice to the enemy is take cover. noted

# ======================= Hibernia =======================
@realm hib

@topic hib_healer
@levels 20-50
@scene druid_bard_warden
@role B class=Druid
@role C class=Bard
@role D class=Warden
A: druid, bard or warden as the group healer?
B: druid, the heals are biggest and the pet helps in a pinch
C: bard heals and mezzes and gives speed, thats three jobs
D: warden can heal and still take a hit in melee
B: three jobs means none done perfectly
C: none done perfectly beats one done alone
A: two of the three then. bard always

@topic bard
@levels 20-50
@scene bards_do_everything
@role B class=Bard
@role C type=NoLifer
A: why is every hib group built around a bard?
B: speed home, mez on the adds, heals in a pinch. we do it all
C: and you get focused first in every fight because of it
B: which means im important
C: which means you die first
A: protect the bard, always

@topic enchanter_pbae
@levels 20-50
@scene enchanter_pbae
@role B class=Enchanter
@role C type=Leveler
A: is enchanter area damage too strong in dungeons?
B: pull the room to me and watch it vanish
C: until something resists and the whole room eats you
B: thats what the bard's mez is for
C: and what the druid's rez is for
A: pull carefully then, and stand near the druid

@topic hib_tanks
@levels 20-50
@scene hero_champ_bm
@role B class=Hero
@role C class=Champion
@role D class=Blademaster
A: hero, champion or blademaster for the front?
B: hero, the shield and the spear hold anything
C: champion, my debuffs make the whole group hit harder
D: blademaster, two blades and the damage to end it
B: and who takes the hits while you both do damage?
C: you, obviously
A: one of each, its a party

@topic animist
@levels 20-50
@scene animist_shrooms
@role B class=Animist
@role C type=NoLifer
A: animists, great keep defenders or just turret lag?
B: plant the shrooms on the walls and nobody gets near the door
C: and the frame rate drops to nothing
B: a slow enemy is a dead enemy
C: a slow ally is also a dead ally
A: shrooms on the walls, effects off, everyone happy

@topic hib_dungeons
@levels 15-25
